chunks.representation:
$$R = \frac{V}{I} \qquad V = IR \qquad I = \frac{V}{R}$$

- units: $\Omega$ (resistance), V (voltage), A (current); $1\ \Omega = 1\ \mathrm{V/A}$;
- large $R$ → small current; small $R$ → large current;
- pushing charge through $R$ dissipates energy as heat.

- individual resistance: property of one component;
- total (equivalent) resistance: what the whole network 'looks like' to the battery;
- series: $R_{total} = R_1 + R_2 + \ldots$ (bigger than any one);
- parallel: $\dfrac{1}{R_{total}} = \dfrac{1}{R_1} + \dfrac{1}{R_2} + \ldots$ (smaller than the smallest).
